# Email templates

When adding or changing outbound email, create a new template pair. Do not inline HTML or long email copy in services.

- Add `app/emails/templates/<name>.html` and `app/emails/templates/<name>.txt`
- Table-based HTML, inline CSS, 560px content width, Arial/Helvetica. This is a transactional email, not an app UI.
- Placeholders are `{{key}}`. Render with `render_email(name, **context)` then `send_email(to, subject, text, html)`.
- Escape happens in the renderer for HTML. Never put OTP codes or secrets in API responses.

```python
# BAD — body built in the service
await send_email(user.email, "Code", f"Your code is {code}")

# GOOD
text, html = render_email("otp", first_name=first_name, code=code, expire_minutes=10, contact_url=FRONTEND_ORIGIN)
await send_email(user.email, "Your SkillQuest verification code", text, html)
```
